<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afonso I of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1109–<a href="/years/1185">1185</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Afonso Henriques, Afonso the Conqueror</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-kongo">Afonso I</a> of Portugal, known as Afonso Henriques, was the first king of Portugal. Son of Count Henry of the County of Portugal, he took power in 1128, proclaimed himself king after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ourique">Battle of Ourique</a> in 1139 and was recognised by León in 1143 and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> in 1179. With crusader help he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> in 1147.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Afonso I of Portugal" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D._Afonso_Henriques_-_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes_(Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
